        "date": "2026-11-21T12:01:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sketch): read selection heights on a DXF sketch fresh outside display\n\nselection_z_range sampled the sketch Z span through the Z_MEMO frame\ncache on every path, including generation and the post gate\n(resolve_params -> selection_base). The frame-cost rule forbids the post\ngate to read a display cache.\n\nThe sketch span is now sampled fresh by default. Only the UI display\nreads (height_memo, boundary marks, manual slot preview, shown region\nlevels) enter operation::display_heights, where the frame memo is used.\n\nPinned by sketch_memo::tests::selection_heights_on_a_sketch_read_fresh_outside_the_display_scope\nand the still-frame sketch_z_fresh_reads assertion in\ncontour_dxf_sketch::sketch_frame_caches_skip_still_frames_and_track_changed_inputs.\n\nRefs #1864\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
